  "result": "Excellent! All tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Payment Terms Implementation\n\n**src/invoices.js** \u2014 Updated `createInvoice` to support payment terms:\n\n- **New helper function `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)`** \u2014 Calculates due dates based on:\n  - **NET14**: 14 days after issue date\n  - **NET30**: 30 days after issue date (default when no terms specified)\n  - **EOM**: Last day of the month of the issue date\n\n- **Updated `createInvoice` signature** \u2014 Accepts optional `terms` parameter. Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on all invoices. Defaults to NET30 if not provided.\n\n- **Error handling** \u2014 Returns `TERMS_INVALID` for unknown terms (case-sensitive, must be exact match: 'NET14', 'NET30', or 'EOM')\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added error code:\n- `TERMS_INVALID`: For unrecognized payment terms\n\n**test/invoices.test.js** \u2014 12 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Default NET30 behavior\n- All three term types (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n- Month and year boundary crossing\n- EOM edge cases (last day of month, February with different leap year scenarios)\n- Invalid terms rejection\n- Proper storage in returned invoice object\n\nAll 140 tests pass (128 existing + 12 new terms tests).",
